  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Afternoon shower and thunderstorm activity each afternoon\n   through early next week.\n\n-  Warming and drying latter part of next week under a ridge of\n   high pressure.\n\n\nSouthwest flow will continue over the region today with a very\nsubtle disturbance moving through the Northern Rockies. This\ndisturbance will help kick off showers and thunderstorms in north\ncentral Idaho and then track into west central and southwest\nMontana. These storms will be capable of producing moderate to\nheavy rainfall, small hail and lightning. \n\nA weak ridge of high pressure builds over the region on Sunday,\nbut enough lingering low level moisture will allow for the\ndevelopment of isolated storms during the afternoon and evening. \nThis ridge of high pressure will persist into Monday but the\nmodels diverge on the extent of the afternoon storm development. \n\nOn Tuesday, a low amplitude trough moves into the Pacific\nNorthwest causing the flow to be flattened over the Northern\nRockies. The westerly flow will allow for another round of\nafternoon convection. Then Wednesday through Friday a ridge of\nhigh pressure is expected to build over the region causing a\nwarming and drying trend.",
